{"title":"2017 CEMC Euclid Problems/Problem 2c Part ii","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_2c\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2c</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2c\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_2c\" title=\"2017 CEMC Euclid Problems/Problem 2c\">Problem 2c</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_2c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2c\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_2c_Part_ii&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Determine one pair <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/e/28e24c43456d95b5ab8d4f2f8f85a644e98b7ed3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a, b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> of positive integers for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/5/735b4fd08c7f1e4d6d79c161a483417073efb9b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/b/85b4a5f389c4da2b8d2b22498db71d019317eb9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/4/7e43689be2523b3fc0903519deab470fcfd7953c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab = 9559$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"80\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_2c_Part_ii&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_2c_Part_i\" title=\"2017 CEMC Euclid Problems/Problem 2c Part i\">part i</a>, we can use difference of squares, the prime factorization of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/0/0b0fefb1817af4845305dfb67d9008a5b2aed0b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9559$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, and the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> being <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/5/f25d31faf472ddb4c698a14522fe8125c06f8dd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> to get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/3/73377f31951b913dffa166d105f9cf3346567ed9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(100 - 21)(100 + 21) = 9559 = 121 \\times 79$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"318\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>This means that we can let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/f/faf07084730bbf0f9f0b0b5691db79808ef5629d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 121$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"63\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/3/2137bfc928ac05b8774a24c7ddfc9191a50996bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 79$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" />, meaning that one possible pair is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/f/aaf9e731d94594fa2fa7612e5a613b184107e15e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(121, 79)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"81\" height=\"32\" />. We can also switch <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/3/80333ecd3dc54cc0d954dd69a682b2b65511f35b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab = ba$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/8/ea872b7bb70f603e02d2990404141d7e8d914709.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(79, 121)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"81\" height=\"32\" /> is also a valid pair.\n</p><p>If we used <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Difference_of_squares\" title=\"Difference of squares\">difference of squares</a> to solve part i, we could have also just used our result there to solve this.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_2c_Part_ii&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The divisibility rule for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> states that the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Alternating_sum\" title=\"Alternating sum\">alternating sum</a> of the digits of a number must be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> for that number to be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/0/1d0ca8a06d79f5bd8825d5ec241205d8bb8c20f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 - 5 + 5 - 9 = 4 - 4 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"203\" height=\"15\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/0/0b0fefb1817af4845305dfb67d9008a5b2aed0b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9559$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> must be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. This means that we can let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/6/ae6b76fe12eefdedbf582848c722f91181b5f595.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"14\" /> and divide by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/0/0b0fefb1817af4845305dfb67d9008a5b2aed0b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9559$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/9/5a9b77bbef493f7effa2ba8d566a4c05143b55f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = \\frac{9559}{11} = 869$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"126\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>This means that one possible pair would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/7/7d7026bd77e5784bab6ab874c1e5f12cca48c028.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(11, 869)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"81\" height=\"32\" />. We can also switch <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/3/80333ecd3dc54cc0d954dd69a682b2b65511f35b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab = ba$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/4/2c4a6c53b83b5f1ea4af4e22cb0ebe98372422f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(869, 11)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"81\" height=\"32\" /> is also a valid pair.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018003532\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.018 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.031 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 141/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 80/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5703/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.302      1 2017_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_2c\n100.00%    6.302      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:35977:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018003532 and revision id 279548. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}